Finally, after 5 years of playing nethack on and off, I've been able
to ascend one of the many, many chaotic orcish wizards I like to play
with. Real-time play was a few hours (2/3) every day for slightly less
than a week; first time a character was able to survive that long :)

I don't have all the technical stats here at this computer, so I'll
try to reconstruct the events as good as I can. Revioli, the oricish
wizard finds himself in the dark dungeons and checks what the good
folks from home have been so kind to give him to aid him on his way:
- the usual stuff (MR cloak, quarterstaff, some mediocre scrolls,
spellbook of force bolt)
- spellbook of identify!!!! (you know the RNG is smiling upon you :D )
- magic marker (0:75-ish) (the only one I "found" in the dungeon)

Some close calls on the first few levels, but found high boots,
studded leather armor, ordinary gloves, a +2 dwarven helmet. First did
the gnomish mines till I hit minetown. Somehow, I also got together a
decent amount of cash (about 9000 Zm) and purchased some protection
from the resident priest (not co-aligned :( ). My AC was about -1 at
this point, so I decided to go for sokoban to get the BoH (mostly
seems to be that, in my games).

I also just recently started playing wizards with daggers and although
it doesn't do much in the late game (I found it to much of a hastle to
run around to pick the daggers up), it does help to keep a fragile
wizards alive during the early game (not to mention trains your dagger
skills for my all-time favourite weapon, Magicbane :) ).

Down we went, me and my pet cat and dog at that point, I guess. I had
found a magic whistle in the gnomish mines, which is a lifesaver for a
wizard, because you can easily keep your pets close (HP) and don't
lose any time going level to level (food, ok less of a problem at this
point).

Every time I got enough mana, I would cast identify (which was at 85%
spell failure at that point), untill I was able to enhance the
relevant spell-casting skill. That's where the real fun kicked in; I
identified everything I came across (although even deep down in
Gehennom, I still found unknown items ...).

So, me, my pets and BoH, go up ... and down to mines end. Found the
usual luck stone there. At this point, the character was around level
12 himself and had found quite some spellbooks (create monster, extra
healing, haste self, ...). I went down untill I hit the level with the
portal to home, but decided to do some altar camping to get Magicbane
and some luck.

Some sacrifices later, Magicbane was acquired, luck was max-ed out and
I think I got Frostbrand around the same time (not sure, never used
it). Going against some spoilers, I enchanted MB up to +5, was not in
the mood to try to get it to +6/+7.

Thanks to the identify spell, I had identified an amulet of reflection
somewhere in the gnomish mines, so I felt somewhat ready to venture
further down. An uncursed ring of levitation brought me side-to-side
Medusa, which I promptly dispatched. One maze level between medusa and
the castle, nothing much to report.

Around this time I had found a few more extremely interesting
spellbooks (teleport away, polymorph!!!!, and lots lots more) but most
were still at an uncomfortable spell failure rate. I used a blessed
scroll of genocide to eliminate all L's.

Approached the castle from the back entrance, as usual. Fought my way
through some hordes of mean beasties, found the wand wished for SDSM
(already had reflection, but I like something else in my amulet
slot). Recharging the wand of wishing using a blessed scroll of
charging brought it to 1:3.

AC was around -10 at this point (bought some more protection along the
way). So with my amulet slot freed, I ventured to do the quest. XP
level was around 14/15 at this point, so had no real problems. The
Dark One had annoyed me a few times the previous games by going up a
few levels before I could reach him, but this time I jumped on the <
when he teleported next to me in the vicinity of the <.

Croaking soon ensued :) Let's see: wandered around the dundeon, did
some more altar camping, found some potions of gain level, blessed
them; eventually reached XP level 19-ish and was finally able to cast
most spells without problems.

My pets were an orange dragon (150 HP), a large dog (?  HP). My own
state at that point in time was around 200 HP and 150 PWR. I decided
to go and polypole some (spellbook of magic mapping!  and dig! :) ). A
looong story short: ended up XP level 21, 270 HP (due to some
wandering nurses), 207 PWR. Altar camping also left me crowned and
with the FoD.

At this point, I felt comfortable entering the VotD and subsequently
Gehennom. Thanks to the teleport and magic mapping spell, it was a
most enjoyable experience :).

The furthest I previously had gotten was acquiring the Candelabrum and
finding the VS, but I bit the dust in Rodney's zoo due to a stoning
attack by a sergeant (????, most have been a thrown egg or
something). anyhow ...

This time, fought Asmodeus (just to see how tough he was; turns out,
not so tough :) ), bribed Baalz. Teleported where I could to the down
stairs, spell-dugg elsewhere to save time (the amulet from the quest
is extremely usefull here :) ). Saw almost no baddies on the way
down. Dug through Juibilex, killed some green slimes.

Found Vlad's tower, got hold of the Candelabrum without any
problems. Ventured down to the lowest level, found the VS easily. Next
was the part I had been dreading because of my previous encounter with
Rodney's zoo, but apart from some summon nasties by a small winged
demon (&, forgot it's name) all went well.

Rodney was no problemo with FoD, he returned once in the dungeon and
once on the plane of earth, both times, the finger did him in :)

As I said, it was the first time that I actually got this far. So
Moloch's sanctum was very exciting, although I got caught in summoning
storm by the same & as in Rodney's zoo. The high priest got the
finger, the level was cleared out for the rest, so I started my
ascension. The mysterious force hit me numerous times and me and my
only remaining pet got seperated :(

I eventually reached the top level, re-read the fading spells and
entered earth. Halfway through, an Archon came to greet me (I had
already seen one this game on level 5 on my way back up). He fell
rather easily once I got my blindfold on, but left quite a nasty heap
of critters :S

Air called for my first use of the ring of conflict, and boy was I
happy to have done that! Even with all of them fighting each other, I
was still swallowed and hit hard by an air elemental. (to find the
portal, I used the last gold detection scroll)

On fire, my magic missiles suddenly became fading, so I read the book
again, only to have it fade :S ... wrote the book again on that
plane(!), wrote a gold detection scroll and off we went :)

Astral plane was again very exciting; I first entered the middle
temple, because Death was guarding it. Unfortunately it turned out to
be neutral :S. Then I turned left to famine, and there my altar stood.

Looked around one last time, said hasta la vista, offered the amulet
and the rest is history :)

There you go, I hope it wasn't too boring for some of you :)

